{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1733"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge sport-games/olympics","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/sport-games__olympics.g1.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",250],["-","stomach,"],["+","stomach"],["=",1],["+","– wrestlers traditionally skip breakfast altogether – then "],["=",118],["+","Wrestlers of a very different build compete on the steppes of Mongolia, where bökh – „firmness“ – is one of the three manly skills alongside horsemanship and archery. Its roots may be the oldest of any sport here: cave paintings in Bayankhongor Province, about 9,000 years old, show two men grappling in front of spectators. Genghis Khan valued wrestling as military training, and today thousands of wrestlers meet at the Naadam festival every July. They wear the zodog, a tight jacket open at the chest, and lose as soon as a knee, an elbow or the back touches the ground.\n\n"],["=",772],["+","Bökh | Mongolia | Bökhchuud | not Olympic |\n| "],["=",79]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",222],["-","Magen,"],["+","Magen"],["=",1],["+","– das Frühstück lassen die Ringer traditionell ganz aus –, danach "],["=",96],["+","Ringer von ganz anderem Körperbau kämpfen in den Steppen der Mongolei, wo Bökh – „Festigkeit“ – neben Reiten und Bogenschießen zu den drei männlichen Künsten zählt. Seine Wurzeln reichen vielleicht am weitesten zurück: Höhlenmalereien in der Provinz Bajanchongor, rund 9.000 Jahre alt, zeigen zwei Männer im Ringkampf vor Zuschauern. Dschingis Khan schätzte das Ringen als militärisches Training, und heute treffen sich jeden Juli Tausende Ringer beim Naadam-Fest. Sie tragen den Zodog, eine enge, vorn offene Jacke, und verlieren, sobald Knie, Ellbogen oder Rücken den Boden berühren.\n\n"],["=",704],["+","Bökh | Mongolei | Bökhchuud | nicht olympisch |\n| "],["=",77]]}]},
